{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"220","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Little Elephant and Problem"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Little Elephant has got a problem — somebody has been touching his sorted by non-decreasing array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" of length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and possibly swapped some elements of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Little Elephant doesn't want to call the police until he understands if he could have accidentally changed the array himself. He thinks that he could have accidentally changed array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", only if array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be sorted in no more than one operation of swapping elements (not necessarily adjacent). That is, the Little Elephant could have accidentally swapped some two elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help the Little Elephant, determine if he could have accidentally changed the array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", sorted by non-decreasing, himself."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2 ≤ n ≤ 105)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the size of array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":". The next line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" positive integers, separated by single spaces and not exceeding "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109"},{"kind":"text","text":", — array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the elements of the array are not necessarily distinct numbers."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In a single line print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without the quotes) if the Little Elephant could have accidentally changed the array himself, and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without the quotes) otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"YES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n3 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"YES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n4 3 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"NO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample the array has already been sorted, so to sort it, we need 0 swap operations, that is not more than 1. Thus, the answer is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample we can sort the array if we swap elements 1 and 3, so we need 1 swap operation to sort the array. Thus, the answer is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third sample we can't sort the array in more than one swap operation, so the answer is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"220A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/220/problem/A"}